# rsdl-appendix-a

The rsdl reference Appendix A as a workspace, every file as the reference writes
it. The manifest names the package `veh`, which holds no source; its
subdirectories are the packages `veh.common`, `veh.adas`, `veh.diag` and
`veh.topology` (ADR-0002 §1), at the paths the reference gives below `veh/`.

The entry checks with no error. Its diagnostics snapshot records the three
warnings the example lists: RSDL-409 twice, for `Panel`'s and `Backend`'s
`requires CruiseControl`, and RSDL-804 once, for `linux.cpuset`, because no
command driver claims a backend namespace yet (plan decision P-B4). The IR,
Rust and TypeScript snapshots are the four packages' own artifacts. The system
snapshot is the lowered system (rsdl reference §13), as `ridlc build --emit
ir-json` writes it to `veh.topology.Vehicle.system.json`: the facts the
reference lists after the example — the closure and its instances, the links of
`Bench` and `Production` with their crossing kinds, the three `Backend` links in
each surface set, the grants, and the installation of `Adas` and `Hmi` — are
all in it. The deployments are in file order, so `Bench` comes first.
